From: GloriousEggroll <gloriouseggroll@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] d3d9: Disable constant buffer streaming for StarCraft II on
 Navi 10 only.

StarCraft II intermittently hung the GPU on RADV with an RX 5700 XT
(Navi 10), and d3d9.deviceLocalConstantBuffers = False avoided it (#790).
That was applied as an application profile for every GPU, but on an
RX 7900 GRE the same setting makes the game freeze during coop, reliably
across several sessions, while Auto does not (#845).

Only default to False for SC2.exe and SC2_x64.exe on AMD Navi 10 device
IDs (0x7310-0x731f), and only while the option is Auto, so setting it
to True or False still wins. Other GPUs keep DXVK's default.
The underlying failure has not been bisected.

Bug: https://github.com/GloriousEggroll/proton-ge-custom/issues/790
Bug: https://github.com/GloriousEggroll/proton-ge-custom/issues/845
---
--- a/src/d3d9/d3d9_options.cpp
+++ b/src/d3d9/d3d9_options.cpp
@@ -1,3 +1,6 @@
+#include <cctype>
+
+#include "../util/util_env.h"
 #include "../util/util_math.h"
 
 #include "d3d9_options.h"
@@ -66,6 +69,23 @@
     this->enumerateByDisplays           = config.getOption<bool>        ("d3d9.enumerateByDisplays",           true);
     this->cachedWriteOnlyBuffers        = config.getOption<bool>        ("d3d9.cachedWriteOnlyBuffers",        false);
     this->deviceLocalConstantBuffers    = config.getOption<Tristate>    ("d3d9.deviceLocalConstantBuffers",    Tristate::Auto);
+
+    /* StarCraft II hangs the GPU with constant buffer streaming on an RX 5700 XT
+     * (Navi 10, GE #790), but disabling it freezes the game in coop on an
+     * RX 7900 GRE (GE #845), so only disable it on Navi 10. Setting
+     * d3d9.deviceLocalConstantBuffers to True or False still wins. */
+    if (this->deviceLocalConstantBuffers == Tristate::Auto && adapter != nullptr) {
+      std::string exe = env::getExeName();
+      const auto info = adapter->info();
+
+      for (auto& c : exe)
+        c = std::tolower(static_cast<unsigned char>(c));
+
+      if ((exe == "sc2.exe" || exe == "sc2_x64.exe")
+       && info.vendorId == 0x1002 && info.deviceId >= 0x7310 && info.deviceId <= 0x731f)
+        this->deviceLocalConstantBuffers = Tristate::False;
+    }
+
     this->allowDirectBufferMapping      = config.getOption<bool>        ("d3d9.allowDirectBufferMapping",      true);
     this->forceDrawTimeBufferUpload     = config.getOption<bool>        ("d3d9.forceDrawTimeBufferUpload",     false);
     this->ignoreDefaultBufferLockRange  = config.getOption<bool>        ("d3d9.ignoreDefaultBufferLockRange",  false);
